Bonjour Managers,

Luc Patoine from Compaq/Digital customer support found our problem:

===========>

>>The bottom line is that 4.0d does not like wide scsi addressing (4.0b just 
ignored it).
>>Wide scsi support will come in Steel (V5.0) of Unix.

>> The syntax to change the hsz70 scsi targets is.. 

>> hsz70> set this id=(0,1,2,3)
>> hsz70> restart other
>>hsz70> restart this

>> This change will be required for all Unix systems with hsz70 controllers
>> upgraded to 4.0d .

<============

My initial problem was that after upgrading to 4.0d I had a 4100 machine that 
crash upon booting  and
another one was not seeing some scsi devices.    Both machine would crash when 
trying
to boot from the CD 4.0D but were ok with 4.0B

SO before upgrading to 4.0d verify that you dont have SCSI id higher than 7 
defined on our HSZ70 controller,
because you'll have some bizzarre problems.


Good luck to all of you and special thank's to Luc Patoine.

Guillaume


