The real problem is that I simply need more memory for those 
memoryintensive FE solvers.

But there were also some other very useful hints:

- A virtual memory problem in DU 4.0D could be fixed with the patch 
vm_perform_v40dbl11.

- There is no way to "reserve" some of the memory for the X Window
System. A solution would be tu run the solver on a different system.

- Very handy is the sys_check utility from the DEC ftp site
ftp.digital.com:/pub/DEC/IAS/sys_check.
 
I ran that and was very surprised how badly configured my system is. 
Perhaps, some new kernel parameters would help me in some way, but I 
think I really need to buy more memory.
