Hi,

I got one fast reply from torben.leifsen@astro.uio.no who said:

   xdpyinfo -display :0.0 | grep Pseudo gives the following output:

       class:    PseudoColor
       class:    PseudoColor

   (card set up with 8 bit depth. We mostly run these cards with 24 bit
    depth)

So the card apparently has two simultaneous PseudoColor visuals. 

Then I've asked him:

  > Thanks for your reply. Looks as if this card has got two simultaneous
  > PseudoColor visuals. What is your impression of the card? How is
  > the video quality and speed when compared to others?

  For 2D purposes it looks good. For 3D it's useless as no OpenGL is
  implemented in hardware. The new PowerStorm 300/350 is probably the best
  choice here.

  For 2D/8-bit applications it seems like a good card. One user complained
  about slow performance with 24-bit with backing-store and save-under
  enabled. When we turned this off the performance was reasonable.

  The video quality appears to be good.

  All in all it seems to be a cheap way to get 24 bit 2D graphics at 
  1280x1024/75 Hz. It certainly has its limitations, but the price is low.

As I don't need 3D OpenGL and the xdpyinfo indicates that the card
supports two simultaneous PseudoColor visuals, I'll probably switch
to this card.

Thanks again to torben.leifsen@astro.uio.no for his reply.

Tom
