Summary
=======

Thanks to 'Bert.Deknuydt@esat.kuleuven.ac.be' for his assistant in setting the
VIC for video conferencing system on AlphaStation 200 system.

The Video conferencing software (VAT, VIC etc) will work on either DEC
TurboChannel or PCI bus architecture.

For PCI bus architecture (AlphaStation 200), it will require the MME subset
installed and 'mmeserver' is running and VIC must compile with 'grabber-mme.o'
object file. The MME subset is on 'Digital Unix Software Product Library CD -
October 1998'.

Bert has put a copy of the VIC binary & source files on:

ftp://ftp.esat.kuleuven.ac.be/pub/psi/visics/deknuydt/vic.gz (1.3 M)

and

ftp://ftp.esat.kuleuven.ac.be/pub/psi/visics/deknuydt/vicsrc-2.8.tar.gz (600 k)

I also found a copy of VIC binary (October 1996) which works on AlphaStation
200 on 'Digital Unix Freeware Executables CD - December 1997'


The VIC source files can be downloaded from 'http://www.video.ja.net/mice/'.
The binary on this site is normally complied with J300 device driver and is
only useful for system with J300 video controller. 


