Hello fellow admins,

We have just purchased a duplexer for our HP1400N postscript printer. We
wish to know what filters to use to enable duplexing. Ideally, we would
like to have one printer queue which accepts duplex and one-sided print
requests. For example,
	lpr -Plp5 -K2 file.ps		(for duplex)
or	lpr -Plp5 file.ps		(for one sided)

If this is not possible, we can certainly add another printcap entry for
duplex printing. From the tru64-unix-managers archive, for this case the
simplest way to achieve duplexing is to insert the following after the
postscript header:
	statusdict begin true setduplexmode end
How can I do this? Refer to URL for more info:
http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/alpha-osf-managers/1995/08/msg00510.html

If you have any information or advice I will summarise.

Regards,
