From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Mar 18 14:40:55 1999
From: jreed () wukon ! appliedtheory ! com
Date: Thu, 18 Mar 1999 14:40:55 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: How to set thresholds in DECevent?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079038515766

I received one very helpful response from Bryan Lavelle, indicating that
I was using the wrong switch to try to set thresholds. His response is 
below. 

- - ------- Forwarded Message

RZ_DISK is a device type, not a device name, therefore you must use

dia set thr -t RZ_DISK -s hard -c 1  OR
dia set thr -t UNSUP_DSK -s hard -c 1  instead of
dia set thr -n RZ_DISK -s hard -c 1

to set the thresholds across the type, not the individual devices.  My
research indicates that RZ type drives are not yet supported in DECevent
under the feature you are trying to implement.

Use "dia shw typ" to view the supported device types.
 
Bryan

- - ------- End of Forwarded Message

