From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Mar 10 16:24:44 1999
From: Don Becker <becker () panther ! adelphi ! edu>
Date: Wed, 10 Mar 1999 16:24:44 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] Audio on 433au under DU4.0c
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079038515592

My original question was how to get audio working on a Personal Workstation 433au
under DU 4.0c

Thanks to:

Peter Stern
Per Boussard
Steve VanDevender

The solution: upgrade Multimedia Services to v2.4, and rebuild the kernel:

> From: Peter Stern <peter@wiscpa.weizmann.ac.il>

> I had this problem once.  In the end, the solution was to install Multimedia
> Services V2.3 or 2.4 (V2.2 doesn not work).  You need: MMEDRVMMSESS241 installed
> Personal Workstation Audio (ES1888/7) Device Support V2.4A(Hardware Option
> Support for PCI/EISA/ISA Bus Machines) in addition to mmeserver (MMERT241).
 
Per also suggested editing configuration info:

> From: Per Boussard <per@era-t.ericsson.se>

> [...] you would want to make sure that /opt/MME241/driver_MMEDRV*/OSF*/isa_data
> contains FUNCTION=ES1888. If you add that, make sure you rebuild the kernel.

I did both, and it works.

--Don

