From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Mar 11 10:22:30 1999
From: tsh () mrc-lmb ! cam ! ac ! uk (T !  S !  Horsnell)
Date: Thu, 11 Mar 1999 10:22:30 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: KZPCM dual-port SCSI problem
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079038515613

Two replies here:

Viktor reminded me that UltraScsi needs a blue shelf to work, which I have.

Alan Rollow suggested that the rz man pages strongly implied that
I should be doing raw disk transfers with record sizes in multiples
of the disk sector size, and that if I modifed my test to do that and
it worked, then the controller would be safe to use for block I/O as
he believed that the rz driver always drove the filesystem in that mode. 
I did modify the test, and it has so far run for 12 hours without failure.
It repeatedly died after about 3 before.

Terry.

